# D2: D1 with the quad OFF (c2-packed-tp4-gate-pairs: QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=0, the same audits and QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all).
# The same four tests, so the difference between D1 and D2 is the flag: in concurrent4_steady the four steady users draft as two
# packed PAIRS (the pair fold at 8 query / 2 KV heads per chip, S2T-07 host-ported and flag-on in the four-card profiles, but never run
# on a card: R0 of the drafting diagnosis), every pair audited against its members' singles. This is both the control for D1 and
# the first hardware run of the pair path at four cards; a failure here says the pair fold (not the quad) is wrong at 8 / 2 heads,
# which the quad's own fold shares (the quad's SDPA is the pair fold's program at 32 / 8 heads over 2,080 keys, per unit).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card batched-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image D0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min (the kernels are cached by D1, but the pair fold's shapes are new: the
# first pair build JIT-compiles inside its round, 0.1-0.5 s once); the four tests 10-15 min: 15 / 35 / 80 min.
# Read: as D1 with the pairs in place of the quad: NO '[PINDIAG] quad draft engaged' line and no '[QUAD-DRAFT]' line; the
# '[PINDIAG] pair row exact engaged pair=[0,1] ... heads=16/4' marker (the pair fold at 8 / 2 heads folded to 16 / 4); '[PACKED-SELECT]
# round=N pairs=[[0, 1], [2, 3]] users=4' in concurrent4_steady and one '[DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] round=N group=[0, 1] ... equal=1'
# plus one for group=[2, 3] per audited round; the round's early_draft and prepare_proposals in [PHASE] against D1's.
# SOFT: a failure does not stop the window (the quad does not need the pairs at run time); its product is the pair measurement. The
# smoke step still ENFORCES the stop conditions (an unequal audit line, garbage text, an errored stream, and that at least one round
# was served by two packed pairs): read the failing line before D3.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-draft-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-pairs
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
